$ greet --help
usage: greet NAME [--times N] [--lang LANG] [--shout] [--help] [--markdown] [--version]

Greet someone, in a few languages

Positional arguments:
  NAME
      Who to greet

Optional switches:
  [1m[36m--times[0m[0m N, [1m[36m-t[0m[0m N
      range [1, 5]
      default value 1
      How many times
  [1m[36m--lang[0m[0m LANG
      choices: en, it, fr
      environment variable name "GREET_LANG"
      default value en
      Language
  [1m[36m--shout[0m[0m
      default value .false.
      Say it louder
  --help, -h
      Print this help message
  --markdown, -md
      Save this help message in a Markdown file
  --version, -v
      Print version
